{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1179525-concerning-ascension","id":1179525,"title":"concerning Ascension","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-26T09:11:03-08:00","id":1179525,"title":"concerning Ascension","content":"so 'ive been reading judgement again and there are a few things that i did not quite understand. i am also under the impression that a lot of things like that were answered back in the day so if anyone remembers that would be great.<br /> <br /> so.. what happens to the universe once ascension happens? after all the tapestry is not just made of humans(and partial humans and former humans etc) normally shouldn't the wheel of ages just continue?<br /> <br /> does the ascended host remain in linear reality or do they move on to the First Age again?<br /> <br /> based on tychoides escaping to another universe i assume that Ascension/the cycle only exists in our prime 9 bubble?<br /> <br /> is ascension mandatory? (i.e can you choose not to ascend if you are like voormas?)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T21:45:11-08:00","id":1179736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1179525-concerning-ascension#post1179525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is ascension mandatory? (i.e can you choose not to ascend if you are like voormas?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I think all the other questions are basically just based on what-if stories as they are written in the old endgame books of when cWoD was supposed to end for good.<br /> So, really, I'd not treat them as anything canon, but possibilities and ideas.<br /> <br /> However, *this* last question was pretty much answered canonically: When the actual ability to Acend becomes available to a Mage, it *is* a choice, much like choice and will is the whole theme of Mage. The best example for beings that decline to Ascend (yet) for whatever Ascension actually means are the Oracles, that decide to remain at the threshold and instead try to guide others towards it. A second example, if somewhat less of one where the choice is concious, are the Exemplars that instead become avatars (not Avatars) of a specific sphere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 01-27-2018, 12:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T07:02:26-08:00","id":1179819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1179525-concerning-ascension?p=1179736#post1179736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally I think all the other questions are basically just based on what-if stories as they are written in the old endgame books of when cWoD was supposed to end for good.<br /> So, really, I'd not treat them as anything canon, but possibilities and ideas.<br /> <br /> However, *this* last question was pretty much answered canonically: When the actual ability to Acend becomes available to a Mage, it *is* a choice, much like choice and will is the whole theme of Mage. The best example for beings that decline to Ascend (yet) for whatever Ascension actually means are the Oracles, that decide to remain at the threshold and instead try to guide others towards it. A second example, if somewhat less of one where the choice is concious, are the Exemplars that instead become avatars (not Avatars) of a specific sphere.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> i was referring to mass Ascension ( i.e when the neverborn turn illusion to truth by consigning it to the unmaking though i see your point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T16:25:40-08:00","id":1179970,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I don't think there is really any actual canonical description of the event, nor its exact nature, and mages disagree what the path towards it is in the first place, so... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I don't think there are real answers. I think it's better that way.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T16:55:58-08:00","id":1179978,"title":"","content":"<b>\u201cThere is a theory which states that if ever anyone discovers exactly what the Universe is for and why it is here, it will instantly disappear and be replaced by something even more bizarre and inexplicable. <br /> <br /> There is another theory which states that this has already happened.\u201d</b><br /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T13:15:30-08:00","id":1180862,"title":"","content":"I thought about the &quot;fascist urge&quot; in mass ascension.<br /> <br /> There's personal gnosis and universal gnosis.<br /> <br /> My Mage character has a very personal view of what enlightenment means, and part of it is the acceptance that other people follow different paths (My Father's House Has Many Rooms and all that), so he's very much against the &quot;fascist urge&quot; of mass-ascension. For him an Ascended universe is just one in which everyone reaches their own personal Gnosis, and the &quot;universal&quot; bit is just something that makes this much more easy without removing exploration or choice.<br /> <br /> For a character who believes in something universalist like traditional Catholic ethics, Universal Ascension is inherently authoritarian, establishing a Pax Romana (heh) and obliterating diversity of belief and practice. I am the way, there is no other way, all that jazz (unless jazz is a sin or something, I don't *think* it is, not fully up to date on the doctrine of the church).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T05:58:49-08:00","id":1181105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1179525-concerning-ascension?p=1180862#post1180862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought about the &quot;fascist urge&quot; in mass ascension.<br /> <br /> There's personal gnosis and universal gnosis.<br /> <br /> My Mage character has a very personal view of what enlightenment means, and part of it is the acceptance that other people follow different paths (My Father's House Has Many Rooms and all that), so he's very much against the &quot;fascist urge&quot; of mass-ascension. For him an Ascended universe is just one in which everyone reaches their own personal Gnosis, and the &quot;universal&quot; bit is just something that makes this much more easy without removing exploration or choice.<br /> <br /> For a character who believes in something universalist like traditional Catholic ethics, Universal Ascension is inherently authoritarian, establishing a Pax Romana (heh) and obliterating diversity of belief and practice. I am the way, there is no other way, all that jazz (unless jazz is a sin or something, I don't *think* it is, not fully up to date on the doctrine of the church).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> hmm, well the final pages of that scenario do says &quot;there is always the one but diversity , the other, is never excluded&quot; obviously this means that the ascended host is not of a single mind but doesn't quite explain what happens to the cosmos or people who may not want to ascend","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T07:43:53-08:00","id":1181124,"title":"","content":"Wasn't there a novel that said something about the Tenth Sphere joining with the others and dissolving the universe into the First Age?.<br /> <br /> If this Ascencion it's Armageddon - like the book suggests - , well, I doubt there's a place to stay after it happens. I also don't think *this* Ascencion it's voluntary - surely Voormas didn't believed so, that's why he wanted to blow up the Tenth Sphere, stop the wheel of time/Armaggedon and all that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T11:22:37-08:00","id":1182992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1179525-concerning-ascension?p=1181124#post1181124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't there a novel that said something about the Tenth Sphere joining with the others and dissolving the universe into the First Age?.<br /> <br /> If this Ascencion it's Armageddon - like the book suggests - , well, I doubt there's a place to stay after it happens. I also don't think *this* Ascencion it's voluntary - surely Voormas didn't believed so, that's why he wanted to blow up the Tenth Sphere, stop the wheel of time/Armaggedon and all that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> so bypassing all the crappiness of the sixth age?(and seventh and eighth and a little bit of ninth) this does raise to question of what happens to non humans(though some books do speak of some spirits remembering the first age)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}